# Windows batch files MUST keep CRLF endings. cmd.exe mis-parses an LF-only
# .cmd — you get errors like "'m' is not recognized" as it chops REM lines —
# and the failure is baffling because the script still half-works. Without this
# rule a build host with core.autocrlf=false (any Linux/macOS CI) would check
# these out as LF and ship a broken launcher.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
